{
  "id": 373075303,
  "iid": 19415,
  "project_id": 7898047,
  "title": "Zabbix: Add capture file output tests",
  "description": "Two sample captures are included at this point, along with the corresponding output text files, for the Python test to work with.\n\nDeveloping Zabbix dissector is somewhat complicated as the Zabbix JSON protocol doesn't have request/response type fields in every message type. Therefore the actual message type (is it a server/proxy/agent/trapper message, is it used in \"active\" or \"passive\" mode, etc) needs to be determined from the other message contents. In a complete capture file it is possible to use the conversation data to improve the message detection, but the goal is to support single-packet captures as well, so meaningful conversation data might not be available. Adding support for new message types may break detection for existing message types.\n\nProviding sample captures and verifying the outputs should help with developing the dissector when the protocol develops over time.\n\nThis first implementation only uses the Info column of the dissection results, other fields could be verified as well if the output file format is made more complex.\n\nThe test is implemented a parametrized test so that each capture file is shown as a separate test in the output. Example output with -v option:\n\n```\ntest/suite_dissectors/group_zabbix.py::TestZabbix::test_zabbix_capture[zabbix70-expression-eval-and-command-requests.pcapng.gz] PASSED\ntest/suite_dissectors/group_zabbix.py::TestZabbix::test_zabbix_capture[zabbix70-large-json.pcapng.gz] PASSED\n```\n\nMore captures are to be added later.",
  "state": "merged",
